# This repository is edited on Windows but runs on a Linux cluster, so every
# text file must keep LF endings in the working tree.  Without this, Git for
# Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks the PBS scripts out with CRLF and the
# cluster fails them with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M".  CRLF in the .dat
# files would also break the byte-identical serial/parallel comparison.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Notebooks and binaries are left exactly as they are.
*.ipynb -text
*.pdf binary
*.pkl binary
